\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Four rigs outside the library with their per-rig adapters (Table~\ref {tab:lora}): one held-out clip per rig, nine frames spread evenly over the clip, prompt quoted. Each panel draws the sample's two decodings, the directly predicted positions (clay) with the forward kinematics of the predicted rotations (teal) over them; a visible separation is a disagreement of the two. Frames are anchored on the root horizontally and keep their world height, the grey line marking the floor height beneath the root; the flying Dragon is anchored in every axis. Clip selection and the unadapted model: App.~\ref {app:qual}.}}{9}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:tb_main}{{3}{9}{Four rigs outside the library with their per-rig adapters (Table~\ref {tab:lora}): one held-out clip per rig, nine frames spread evenly over the clip, prompt quoted. Each panel draws the sample's two decodings, the directly predicted positions (clay) with the forward kinematics of the predicted rotations (teal) over them; a visible separation is a disagreement of the two. Frames are anchored on the root horizontally and keep their world height, the grey line marking the floor height beneath the root; the flying Dragon is anchored in every axis. Clip selection and the unadapted model: App.~\ref {app:qual}}{figure.3}{}}
