\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Tensor flow and training details of the 303M model. Solid arrows carry data or state, dashed arrows conditioning. Left to right: rig and motion tokens with the 17-channel layout and the validity masks; the token embedding and the two conditioning paths (per-joint, and the global vector $\mathbf  c$ that drives AdaLN); the fourteen factorised blocks with the spatial-attention bias; sampling with caption guidance, the 20 Euler steps, de-normalisation and the two decodes. The bottom band lists the training inputs, the grouped Huber objective of Eqs.~(\ref {eq:elem})--(\ref {eq:grouped}), the acceleration term and the three further auxiliary terms.}}{15}{figure.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:model_details}{{4}{15}{Tensor flow and training details of the \num {303}M model. Solid arrows carry data or state, dashed arrows conditioning. Left to right: rig and motion tokens with the 17-channel layout and the validity masks; the token embedding and the two conditioning paths (per-joint, and the global vector $\mathbf c$ that drives AdaLN); the fourteen factorised blocks with the spatial-attention bias; sampling with caption guidance, the 20 Euler steps, de-normalisation and the two decodes. The bottom band lists the training inputs, the grouped Huber objective of Eqs.~(\ref {eq:elem})--(\ref {eq:grouped}), the acceleration term and the three further auxiliary terms}{figure.4}{}}
