\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Truebones arms of Table~\ref {tab:lora}: one held-out clip per rig, six frames spread evenly over the clip, three-quarter view; the quoted sentence is the conditioning prompt. In every panel the directly predicted joint positions (clay) are overlaid by the forward kinematics of the predicted rotations (teal); a visible separation is the projected FK--pose discrepancy (a single view can hide a disagreement in depth). Rows: the library model with the rig's statistics only (\emph  {zero}, the unadapted snapshot, from which every column of that table's \emph  {zero} block is read) and the per-rig adapter (\emph  {LoRA}). Frames are anchored on the root horizontally and keep their height above the floor; the grey line marks the floor height beneath the root. Both rows of a rig are drawn at the same scale. The clip shown is the one of that rig whose adapted sample is closest to the held-out motion; Table~\ref {tab:lora} reports all four rigs over all of their held-out clips.}}{25}{figure.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:tb_filmstrips}{{5}{25}{Truebones arms of Table~\ref {tab:lora}: one held-out clip per rig, six frames spread evenly over the clip, three-quarter view; the quoted sentence is the conditioning prompt. In every panel the directly predicted joint positions (clay) are overlaid by the forward kinematics of the predicted rotations (teal); a visible separation is the projected FK--pose discrepancy (a single view can hide a disagreement in depth). Rows: the library model with the rig's statistics only (\emph {zero}, the unadapted snapshot, from which every column of that table's \emph {zero} block is read) and the per-rig adapter (\emph {LoRA}). Frames are anchored on the root horizontally and keep their height above the floor; the grey line marks the floor height beneath the root. Both rows of a rig are drawn at the same scale. The clip shown is the one of that rig whose adapted sample is closest to the held-out motion; Table~\ref {tab:lora} reports all four rigs over all of their held-out clips}{figure.5}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Two prompts on one rig, in world coordinates. Five frames at equal times of one held-out clip (light first, dark last) with the per-rig adapter of Table~\ref {tab:lora}. Every frame keeps the height the model produced; the horizontal placement is the panel's own time grid, the clay line is the root's height profile through the five frames and the grey line is the floor beneath the root. Skeletons are the deployable output: the forward kinematics of the predicted rotations. The quoted sentence is the conditioning prompt; the two rows of a rig differ in nothing else and are drawn at one scale.}}{26}{figure.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:tb_world}{{6}{26}{Two prompts on one rig, in world coordinates. Five frames at equal times of one held-out clip (light first, dark last) with the per-rig adapter of Table~\ref {tab:lora}. Every frame keeps the height the model produced; the horizontal placement is the panel's own time grid, the clay line is the root's height profile through the five frames and the grey line is the floor beneath the root. Skeletons are the deployable output: the forward kinematics of the predicted rotations. The quoted sentence is the conditioning prompt; the two rows of a rig differ in nothing else and are drawn at one scale}{figure.6}{}}
